bregions ${R}_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y)=3x-8y+6$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=3x-8y+6$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{M}_{ij}=f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=3{x}_{i}-8{y}_{j-1}+6\n$$\n\nand the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(3{x}_{i}-8{y}_{j-1}+6)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $3{x}_{i}-8{y}_{j-1}+6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123740/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89023510-57f4-52f9-90ed-eae07f48f707"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123740"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72909/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer/id #uuid "7f647946-7308-5125-8c30-40bb8c84b6c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72909/selection/5cd5dc93f37c743976373ab57c37b5388ba149bd286c5b2139ed2c89c249424d" :answer/id #uuid "325bae4a-401d-5ab3-a5d4-7869967ea6d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72909/selection/aa4e4239377eb61b8bdf37e9f4374abeb3a1fdeaaf409dc6e37519ad01509799" :answer/id #uuid "0f51c298-6c79-523a-89f5-b85b1928b05e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72909/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "03c20b7f-7a89-5360-ab37-3c1852f54906" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72909/selection/6d8a7c7e73b503e82ee3fdeaeeda8131c0106d9ecb6a16ba218483b62acd0090" :answer/id #uuid "a9034a66-a89e-5bc8-bbcc-74874576e989" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72909/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "25683915-c818-5236-a6fb-4f6aa94c04ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72909/selection/6d8a7c7e73b503e82ee3fdeaeeda8131c0106d9ecb6a16ba218483b62acd0090" :answer-field/choices ["q-72909/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" "q-72909/selection/5cd5dc93f37c743976373ab57c37b5388ba149bd286c5b2139ed2c89c249424d" "q-72909/selection/aa4e4239377eb61b8bdf37e9f4374abeb3a1fdeaaf409dc6e37519ad01509799" "q-72909/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-72909/selection/6d8a7c7e73b503e82ee3fdeaeeda8131c0106d9ecb6a16ba218483b62acd0090"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72909" :question/id #uuid "3d396205-f6a2-5f67-98a9-fdf447376337" :question/math-academy-id "q-72909" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,4]\\times [1,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=-2$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=-2,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-2)\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =-2({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =-2(4-1)(4-1) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 3\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=-18\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le -18=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=-18.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-72909/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72909"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123846/selection/85a3108a003d23ae32c148d83b3c58c683299fe7f8b4da18365678303eb14a49" :answer/id #uuid "d19a0965-6c2b-52aa-9a84-abbbe8217290" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "88" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123846/selection/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" :answer/id #uuid "4954b87e-acd6-5f5e-b91e-3d89f44e1210" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123846/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "6c401d46-b992-59e6-8863-38ecab593c0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123846/selection/eaa0ff3d0e34bf4cc56606f08b4c540c17a85ab3f394397b4f1f6fe3c6d48656" :answer/id #uuid "658ce99c-4f6c-5011-9089-a627ce1ed6bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "108" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123846/selection/bc787d823ec953ec5e44b8f7f4a4c7f3b5de4a6a5f1cea9c5a660d6b5e6faac7" :answer/id #uuid "27ede692-5090-5a91-b029-26c5b6640e95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "96" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123846/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c955686-849b-5d9f-8887-4249163d5c70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123846/selection/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" :answer-field/choices ["q-123846/selection/85a3108a003d23ae32c148d83b3c58c683299fe7f8b4da18365678303eb14a49" "q-123846/selection/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" "q-123846/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-123846/selection/eaa0ff3d0e34bf4cc56606f08b4c540c17a85ab3f394397b4f1f6fe3c6d48656" "q-123846/selection/bc787d823ec953ec5e44b8f7f4a4c7f3b5de4a6a5f1cea9c5a660d6b5e6faac7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123846" :question/id #uuid "f0c22e73-7654-5d07-a6ef-2c5b4606e203" :question/math-academy-id "q-123846" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,7]\\times [4,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=6$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=6,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}6\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =6({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =6(7-1)(6-4) \\\\  & =6\\cdot 6\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=72\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le 72=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=72.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123846/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123846"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123839/selection/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" :answer/id #uuid "4e58385a-6d95-5f4e-b793-41bad8d90d24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123839/selection/5cd5dc93f37c743976373ab57c37b5388ba149bd286c5b2139ed2c89c249424d" :answer/id #uuid "a5566391-5887-5931-ac51-1084acb08df5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123839/selection/008b962e8dba6a793a19582d7b90d25ecc915fb39cdb8821fa797599cabe57ab" :answer/id #uuid "645e7f31-6479-5974-ba9c-59a1593f462b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123839/selection/faf6532f0d4ab903ddc295ac11018acfd3bce2ae030f3f2eed578181eeb5e5e5" :answer/id #uuid "b4780a7b-0675-5cb5-8868-06d94aae8b87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123839/selection/ce9ad5740269388d77893fbd186fe766ceb1482af44117dcfc7940e9dca5a239" :answer/id #uuid "18a37a70-dc7f-5128-98c3-a65ec67c1bab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123839/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "949a5957-0ee7-5504-a207-1f21d67c7892" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123839/selection/5cd5dc93f37c743976373ab57c37b5388ba149bd286c5b2139ed2c89c249424d" :answer-field/choices ["q-123839/selection/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" "q-123839/selection/5cd5dc93f37c743976373ab57c37b5388ba149bd286c5b2139ed2c89c249424d" "q-123839/selection/008b962e8dba6a793a19582d7b90d25ecc915fb39cdb8821fa797599cabe57ab" "q-123839/selection/faf6532f0d4ab903ddc295ac11018acfd3bce2ae030f3f2eed578181eeb5e5e5" "q-123839/selection/ce9ad5740269388d77893fbd186fe766ceb1482af44117dcfc7940e9dca5a239"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123839" :question/id #uuid "4539918d-15a9-5633-94ba-162c54a0312b" :question/math-academy-id "q-123839" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,3]\\times [2,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=-3$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=-3,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-3)\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =-3({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =-3(3-(-1))(5-2) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=-36\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le -36=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=-36.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123839/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123839"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72684/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "979edcc5-f7e9-5d25-a26c-e4f8cc8374a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72684/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "6688d98f-2459-57a7-8b15-e42b4aa215ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72684/selection/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" :answer/id #uuid "d2ddd0a8-0864-5d45-85b7-9628f09deb67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72684/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "3311fecc-a677-57c3-8e01-bcbc3748c7c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72684/selection/772faee3af740960f7d296ca245df4da797a9e413368076cbaa828915d92739d" :answer/id #uuid "82f8c6de-30d9-5961-8ef4-dfb0094d090d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "128" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72684/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ef73560-a1f3-5274-83c1-02d51b804850" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72684/selection/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" :answer-field/choices ["q-72684/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-72684/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-72684/selection/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" "q-72684/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" "q-72684/selection/772faee3af740960f7d296ca245df4da797a9e413368076cbaa828915d92739d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72684" :question/id #uuid "d67b2272-6cb0-5162-9166-f9c0809e3db8" :question/math-academy-id "q-72684" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,4]\\times [2,6]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=4$ for all partition $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=4,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}4\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =4({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =4(4-0)(6-2) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=64\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le 64=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=64.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-72684/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72684"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123843/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "8051af47-5f4a-53a6-9c50-e3c3aad202e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123843/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "bc95eebd-c863-5c9f-a62b-f769557bf4a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123843/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "75d3dcf6-5518-5670-bc83-0f8c216baa26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123843/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "9512f7c7-6c21-5dbd-bbab-8f44e458e852" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123843/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "3883bf7d-2d69-5a5a-802a-eaa5c3bc0052" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123843/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "670398aa-bb0c-52e9-b66b-60a629755f3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123843/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-123843/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-123843/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-123843/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-123843/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-123843/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123843" :question/id #uuid "212d6373-efba-5135-90cc-77b5fcb91a3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-123843" :question/problem "Let $R=[-5,-2]\\times [3,7]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=1$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P),\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand ${m}_{ij}$ and ${M}_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since ${m}_{ij}={M}_{ij}=1,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}1\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =(-2-(-5))(7-3) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=12\\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le 12=U(f,P)\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=12.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123843/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0559f0c-a1ca-5ba8-a02e-71d584273958"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123843"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123872/selection/a56cff9bcd972e5f984cf41a1bd009448de7a7ce0651819ce15780644d1c2587" :answer/id #uuid "2e8a6466-736f-5eab-844e-aafc9912be06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "258" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123872/selection/146ef59b9a85058c08e5f4d772c10028788f315c29fe2290468e61807b6d55f4" :answer/id #uuid "6deac03f-2f77-5460-9cf8-9a2eda2ae86e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "234" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123872/selection/986defab6491c35d63eb6cbb51160fc4661c412829aae69b259657fbcf9ddb8a" :answer/id #uuid "0e2edc8a-35ae-58be-84b6-96386a37db72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "306" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123872/selection/9051bdb0a37deacbd41852a921a411d696ee85cf781f9326c616f643653be20a" :answer/id #uuid "3c79e2da-64d0-57b4-9407-5e76830405e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "162" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123872/selection/407a8c9dd7706a5c0017938bdc16d552cb404ed5280e2197eaee2471cbb5128e" :answer/id #uuid "2d29142b-1a94-5425-b7a7-5778de06d784" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "210" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123872/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d81bd184-da06-5b5c-8a0c-29198780befe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123872/selection/a56cff9bcd972e5f984cf41a1bd009448de7a7ce0651819ce15780644d1c2587" :answer-field/choices ["q-123872/selection/a56cff9bcd972e5f984cf41a1bd009448de7a7ce0651819ce15780644d1c2587" "q-123872/selection/146ef59b9a85058c08e5f4d772c10028788f315c29fe2290468e61807b6d55f4" "q-123872/selection/986defab6491c35d63eb6cbb51160fc4661c412829aae69b259657fbcf9ddb8a" "q-123872/selection/9051bdb0a37deacbd41852a921a411d696ee85cf781f9326c616f643653be20a" "q-123872/selection/407a8c9dd7706a5c0017938bdc16d552cb404ed5280e2197eaee2471cbb5128e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123872" :question/id #uuid "f334c18b-c7f6-5afa-84d2-c8f6b1961318" :question/math-academy-id "q-123872" :question/problem "Let $R=[-4,0]\\times [-5,-2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-2{x}_{i}-5{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-2{x}_{i-1}-5{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n-2{x}_{i}-5{y}_{j}\\le -2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le -2{x}_{i-1}-5{y}_{j-1}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\n-2{x}_{i}-5{y}_{j}\\le -({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-\\frac{5}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le -2{x}_{i-1}-5{y}_{j-1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[-({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-\\frac{5}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & \\le -{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}-\\frac{5}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\le U(f,P).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =({0}^{2}-(-4)^{2})(-2-(-5))=-48 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{5}{2}((-2)^{2}-(-5)^{2})(0-(-4))=-210\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le -(-48)-(-210)\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le 258\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=258.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-123872/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b9d2e98-8007-51ec-bfb6-cb9b48029a2a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123872"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-72627"] :question/problem "Let $R=[0,4]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(4{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(4{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n4\\cdot {x}_{i-1}+2\\cdot {y}_{j-1}\\le 4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 4\\cdot {x}_{i}+2\\cdot {y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\n4{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}\\le 2({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 4{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[2({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le 2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P).\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =2({4}^{2}-{0}^{2})(2-0)=64 \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =({2}^{2}-{0}^{2})(4-0)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le 64+16\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le 80\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=80.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-123873/selection/7810d1304c7bd5d2ee99462143ac50d13c0ef4f6da1eff3e285f45b51aa692f4" :answer/id #uuid "e67ec58f-1203-597c-a93b-4de390e6ce5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-132" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123873/selection/ebfc0e0786b9e08f32fe2539ae50e791a60b7c4613bb2a0820cefbd3ea742454" :answer/id #uuid "2d53385b-3569-5e5f-93a2-e3b933dab12e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123873/selection/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" :answer/id #uuid "9c2f4f5f-ed52-5c84-b5b3-3410387936c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123873/selection/1c35128c59a7847a115977df43414655602222d4153c898daa47f08b0f9b4500" :answer/id #uuid "dc8824b8-8360-5cff-95c5-3b1cfbe5c42f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-96" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123873/selection/5aa7d5a70efa831a31e6b82f10565bd69bbaa8c894b8c1ee39d98f5fac58a077" :answer/id #uuid "12607cb3-376b-5b1f-a3f8-2d29b3a792c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-108" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123873/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c65d2859-f2b1-5a54-9bde-1036012fc28a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123873/selection/ebfc0e0786b9e08f32fe2539ae50e791a60b7c4613bb2a0820cefbd3ea742454" :answer-field/choices ["q-123873/selection/7810d1304c7bd5d2ee99462143ac50d13c0ef4f6da1eff3e285f45b51aa692f4" "q-123873/selection/ebfc0e0786b9e08f32fe2539ae50e791a60b7c4613bb2a0820cefbd3ea742454" "q-123873/selection/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" "q-123873/selection/1c35128c59a7847a115977df43414655602222d4153c898daa47f08b0f9b4500" "q-123873/selection/5aa7d5a70efa831a31e6b82f10565bd69bbaa8c894b8c1ee39d98f5fac58a077"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123873" :question/id #uuid "6290d12e-5625-5378-a1c5-40b0a700fc6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-123873" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,2]\\times [-2,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-3-4{x}_{i}-6{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(-3-4{x}_{i-1}-6{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following results:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0}) \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}-{x}_{0})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3-4{x}_{i}-6{y}_{j} & \\le -3-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j}) \\\\  & \\le -3-4{x}_{i-1}-6{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\n-3-4{x}_{i}-6{y}_{j}\\le -3-2({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-3({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le -3-4{x}_{i-1}-6{y}_{j-1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[-3-2({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})-3({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & \\le -3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\,-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\,-3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\le U(f,P).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =2({2}^{2}-(-1)^{2})(2-(-2))=24 \\\\ 3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =3({2}^{2}-(-2)^{2})(2-(-1))=0 \\\\ 3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =3(2-(-1))(2-(-2))=36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le -36-24-0\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le -60\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=-60.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-123873/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b9d2e98-8007-51ec-bfb6-cb9b48029a2a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123873"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72906/selection/6f6a1a16a9213ceb79e4f2f942541fed384b5370eecb02e6f044b9c47e2cbdc7" :answer/id #uuid "1c914005-a184-5da1-b324-7bd70d67b11d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-360" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72906/selection/dda179d45ca7e4a0613a402c0534e8afa19f93dae661acf79d186d317009e033" :answer/id #uuid "faba89cb-0d0c-5e3d-8492-d28a6a54aa71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-84" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72906/selection/cff7144149d407705650607369c836b0a8a0fe3ec1b651da86c35630cdf8d9c0" :answer/id #uuid "0dc1b137-6504-51a8-9e34-5d6b3f69b157" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-168" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72906/selection/8c174f152865871bf1a4e5b95ecc413096799f99ad4dcb5dcd1578ab55a8ec94" :answer/id #uuid "0c0a18fb-690b-5f67-8274-623c26ea90ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-324" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72906/selection/f866f5392569117b766abfd16deaccde33bf82ab38fb5120d21e4d3e19e6cfef" :answer/id #uuid "ada1ffaf-d18d-5212-9f86-5555bc1f69db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-144" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72906/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9f07878-22a4-50c3-9e66-1bf28f6b3816" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72906/selection/f866f5392569117b766abfd16deaccde33bf82ab38fb5120d21e4d3e19e6cfef" :answer-field/choices ["q-72906/selection/6f6a1a16a9213ceb79e4f2f942541fed384b5370eecb02e6f044b9c47e2cbdc7" "q-72906/selection/dda179d45ca7e4a0613a402c0534e8afa19f93dae661acf79d186d317009e033" "q-72906/selection/cff7144149d407705650607369c836b0a8a0fe3ec1b651da86c35630cdf8d9c0" "q-72906/selection/8c174f152865871bf1a4e5b95ecc413096799f99ad4dcb5dcd1578ab55a8ec94" "q-72906/selection/f866f5392569117b766abfd16deaccde33bf82ab38fb5120d21e4d3e19e6cfef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72906" :question/id #uuid "44ba02d1-09f0-557c-bc39-57987e983b2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-72906" :question/problem "Let $R=[-5,-1]\\times [0,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n5{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}\\le 5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 5{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\n5{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}\\le \\frac{5}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})\\le 5{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{5}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le \\frac{5}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P).\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{5}{2}((-1)^{2}-(-5)^{2})(3-0)=-180 \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =({3}^{2}-{0}^{2})(-1-(-5))=36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le -180+36\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le -144\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=-144.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-72906/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b9d2e98-8007-51ec-bfb6-cb9b48029a2a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72906"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72905/selection/2671fdc3a44bd3421ded09be4e881743067a96eb4e584e442a30f737593eae71" :answer/id #uuid "29d98d56-0dd0-58bb-9328-5f429dbc14ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "38" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72905/selection/7495b22a8694caf4eab331e172464242c9c26d3eafc6582b001b0ab03e9f01a4" :answer/id #uuid "74daab8d-a932-565d-8959-172dac3c88d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "57" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72905/selection/de4adedcb4f94c847122905ee3a7a3f16eecda2d4ce5fbbb83bc1b08e3c95a70" :answer/id #uuid "af81be29-9118-5088-9414-b66bf3328319" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "63" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72905/selection/2fadfe0151f1f25e0ae6e00d2197f0e94fbc34184c655065ac97e6df3ba2d294" :answer/id #uuid "1bd567ed-4f92-540a-afd5-9b49525cc17d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "69" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72905/selection/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" :answer/id #uuid "df386287-2cae-5762-84da-48ae92ab1f6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72905/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bbed1845-521e-523a-9287-a8b1d745c45d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72905/selection/7495b22a8694caf4eab331e172464242c9c26d3eafc6582b001b0ab03e9f01a4" :answer-field/choices ["q-72905/selection/2671fdc3a44bd3421ded09be4e881743067a96eb4e584e442a30f737593eae71" "q-72905/selection/7495b22a8694caf4eab331e172464242c9c26d3eafc6582b001b0ab03e9f01a4" "q-72905/selection/de4adedcb4f94c847122905ee3a7a3f16eecda2d4ce5fbbb83bc1b08e3c95a70" "q-72905/selection/2fadfe0151f1f25e0ae6e00d2197f0e94fbc34184c655065ac97e6df3ba2d294" "q-72905/selection/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72905" :question/id #uuid "6b42d7f7-8e5b-51c7-9711-14914c01cbe0" :question/math-academy-id "q-72905" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,4]\\times [2,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(3{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}-1)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(3{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}-1)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following results:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0}) \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}=({x}_{m}-{x}_{0})({y}_{n}-{y}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le I\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that ${\\overset{¯}{x}}_{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})$ will always lie between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$, and similarly ${\\overset{¯}{y}}_{j}=\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})$ will always lie between ${y}_{j-1}$ and ${y}_{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n3{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}-1\\le 3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})-1\\le 3{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}-1\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\n3{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}-1\\le \\frac{3}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})-1\\le 3{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}-1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}$ and applying the double summation gives:\n\n$$\nL(f,P)\\le {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{3}{2}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})+\\frac{1}{2}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})-1]Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\le U(f,P)\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & \\le \\frac{3}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\,+\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\,-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & \\le U(f,P).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{3}{2}({4}^{2}-{1}^{2})(4-2)=45 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{1}{2}({4}^{2}-{2}^{2})(4-1)=18 \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =(4-1)(4-2)=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le 45+18-6\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le 57\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A=57.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-72905/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b9d2e98-8007-51ec-bfb6-cb9b48029a2a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72905"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9497"] :question/problem "Let $R = [0,1]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 12-x-y.$ Further, let \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle I = \\iint\\limits_{R} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm dA\n$$\n\nbe the unique number such that over all rectangular partitions $P$ of $R,$ we have \n$L(f,P)\\:\\leq I \\:\\leq U(f,P),$\nwhere $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P)$ are the corresponding lower and upper Riemann sums. Write down the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P) \\leq I \\leq U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand $m_{ij}$ and $M_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe need to compute $U(f,P).$ \n\nNotice that for all subregions $R_{ij},$ we have that\n\n- $f(x,y) = 12-x-y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 12-x-y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. Therefore,\n\n$$\nM_{ij} = f(x_{i-1}, y_{j-1}) = 12-x_{i-1}-y_{j-1}\n$$\n\nand the upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P) = \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n (12-x_{i-1}-y_{j-1})\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6122"] :question/problem "Let $R = [-1,4]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the double integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\iint\\limits_R f(x,y) \\, \\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ is a function such that $m_{ij} = M_{ij} = 3$ for all partitions $P$ of $R,$ and $m_{ij}$ and $M_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ respectively in each subregion $R_{ij}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P) \\leq I \\leq U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R,$ where the lower and upper sums respectively are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand $m_{ij}$ and $M_{ij}$ are the minimum and maximum values of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nNow, since $m_{ij}=M_{ij}=3,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =3({\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}) \\\\  & =3(4-(-1))(2-1) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)=15 & \\le {∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\le 15=U(f,P),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich implies that\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_R f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d A = 15.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9494"] :question/problem "Let $R = [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)$ be a function defined over $R.$\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1})\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},\\, \\\\ U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}+2{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f,P)$ and $U(f,P),$ compute $\\displaystyle\\iint\\limits_R f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d A.$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n\\left(x_{i-1} + x_i\\right)\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j = (x_m^2 - x_0^2)(y_n-y_0)\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x,y),$ the double integral of $f$ over a rectangular region $R$ is the unique number $I$ (if it exists) such that\n\n$$\nL(f,P) \\leq I \\leq U(f,P)\n$$\n\nover all partitions $P$ of $R.$\n\nFirst, notice that $\\bar{x}_i = \\dfrac 1 2 (x_{i-1}+x_i)$ will always lie between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i,$ and similarly $\\bar{y}_j = \\dfrac 1 2 (y_{j-1}+y_j)$ will always lie between $y_{j-1}$ and $y_j.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nx_{i-1} + {\\color{blue}2}y_{j-1} \\leq \\dfrac{1}{2}(x_{i-1} + x_i) + {\\color{blue}2}\\cdot \\dfrac 1 2 (y_{j-1} + y_j) \\leq x_{i} + {\\color{blue}2}y_{j},\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to \n\n$$\nx_{i-1} + 2y_{j-1} \\leq \\dfrac{1}{2}(x_{i-1} + x_i) + (y_{j-1} + y_j)\\leq x_{i} + 2y_{j}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying this by $\\Delta x_i\\Delta y_j$ and applying the double summation gives\n\n$$\nL(f,P) \\leq \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n\\left[\\dfrac{1}{2}(x_{i-1} + x_i) + (y_{j-1} + y_j)\\right]\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j\\leq U(f,P).\n$$\n\nSeparating the sums using the addition and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\nL(f,P) \\leq \\dfrac{1}{2}\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n\\left(x_{i-1} + x_i\\right)\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j + \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n\\left(y_{j-1} + y_j\\right)\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j\\leq U(f,P).\n$$\n\nUsing the hint, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+{x}_{i})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =\\frac{1}{2}({2}^{2}-{0}^{2})(3-1)=4 \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}+{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =({3}^{2}-{1}^{2})(2-0)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P)\\le 4+16\\le U(f,P)\\,⟹\\,L(f,P)\\le 20\\le U(f,P)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_R f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d A = 20.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
